  clock: 3  # 7b93
  nonce: 7b93  # 7b93
  message: "DONE in PR #1276 with WI-nunab. os.OpenFile is rowed under fs_read AND fs_write, mode-discriminated like python's open. The flag argument is read by NAME: ModeArgument.flag_modes in io_boundary._MODE_ARGUMENT_POSITIONS['go']; O_WRONLY / O_RDWR / O_APPEND / O_CREATE / O_TRUNC write, O_RDONLY alone reads. go.py now calls the shared stamp_io_mode_from_call. A flag held in a variable stamps nothing and keeps the first-declared fs_read row, the same absence rule as a non-literal mode string. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on merged dev: 'fh, _ := os.OpenFile(p, os.O_WRONLY|os.O_CREATE, 0o644); fh.Write(b)' gives fs_write chains os.OpenFile and os.File.Write, and a must_not_exist fs_write claim moves inconclusive -> VIOLATED; os.O_RDONLY gives fs_read. Tests: test_go_handle_writes.py, core test_mode_from_flag_names.py (5 flag cases). A/B: +17 (beads) and +33 (prometheus) os.OpenFile fs_write chains. A 10-site read-back against source: 9/9 write flags correct, 1 fs_read where the flag was not a literal on the call line."  # 7b93
